       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="VTU Results 2026 Latest Updates">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">VTU Results 2026 Declared: Your Comprehensive Guide to December/January Exam Scores!</h1>
                    <p class="lead mb-4">The wait is over for thousands of students! Visvesvaraya Technological University (VTU) has officially announced the much-anticipated results for the December 2025 and January 2026 examinations. This crucial announcement covers a wide array of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, including B.E, B.Plan, B.Arch, and B.Sc (Hons), all under the Choice Based Credit System (CBCS). If you appeared for these exams, it's time to check your performance and plan your next steps.</p>

                    <div class="highlight-text">
                        <p><strong>Breaking News:</strong> VTU has published the results of the December 2025/January 2026 examinations on March 3, 2026. Students can now access their scorecards online.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Check Your VTU Results 2026 Instantly</h2>
                    <p>Accessing your VTU results is a straightforward process. The university has made the scores available on its official results portal, ensuring a smooth experience for all candidates. Make sure you have your University Seat Number (USN) handy.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official VTU Results Portal</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the official Visvesvaraya Technological University results portal: <a href="https://results.vtu.ac.in" target="_blank">results.vtu.ac.in</a>. This is the primary destination for all VTU examination outcomes.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Select Your Examination Link</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for the specific result link corresponding to the "December 2025/January 2026 Examination". You might also see categories like B.E/B.Tech, MBA, MCA, M.Tech, or B.Sc (Hons). Choose the one relevant to your course and semester.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your USN and Captcha</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">You will be prompted to enter your University Seat Number (USN) and a security captcha. Ensure these details are entered accurately to avoid any retrieval issues. Some portals might also ask for your date of birth.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. View and Download Your Result</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">After entering the required information, click on the "Submit" or "View Result" button. Your detailed scorecard will be displayed on the screen. It is highly recommended to download and save a PDF copy or take a printout for your records and future academic or official references.</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Understanding Your VTU Scorecard</h2>
                    <p>VTU employs an absolute grading system, converting raw marks into grades. Your scorecard will feature essential details such as your semester-wise marks, grades, Semester Grade Point Average (SGPA), and Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA). These metrics are vital for tracking your academic progression and are often required for placements, internships, and further studies.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>CBCS vs. Non-CBCS:</strong> VTU releases results for both Choice Based Credit System (CBCS) and Non-CBCS schemes. Be sure to select the correct tab when checking your results.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Verify All Details:</strong> Upon downloading your scorecard, meticulously check all personal details, subject codes, marks, and grades. Any discrepancies should be reported to the examination authorities immediately.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Post-Result Procedures: Revaluation and Photocopy Applications</h2>
                    <p>For students who are not satisfied with their marks, VTU provides options for revaluation and obtaining photocopies of answer scripts. The university has indicated that information regarding applications for revaluation and photocopies will be issued shortly on the official university notice board.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Applying for a Photocopy of Your Answer Script</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            <p>This is often the first and most crucial step before considering revaluation. Applying for a scanned copy (photocopy) of your answer script allows you to review your paper, identify where marks might have been lost, and then make an informed decision about revaluation.</p>
                            <p><strong>How to Apply:</strong> Applications are typically made online through the VTU results portal (results.vtu.ac.in). A nominal fee is usually charged per subject.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. The Revaluation Process and the 15-Mark Rule</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            <p>Once you've reviewed your photocopy, you can decide whether to apply for revaluation. During revaluation, your answer script is evaluated by a different examiner.</p>
                            <p><strong>The 15-Mark Rule:</strong> This is a critical aspect of VTU revaluation. A change in your marks will only be considered if the difference between your original marks and the revaluation marks is <strong>more than 15 marks</strong>. If the difference is 15 or less, your original marks will be retained. If the difference is 16 or more, the average of the two scores will be awarded as your new marks.</p>
                            <p><strong>Application &amp; Fees:</strong> Revaluation applications are also submitted online, with a separate, higher fee per subject, which is generally non-refundable.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Challenge Revaluation</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            <p>For students who are extremely confident of a major error in evaluation, Challenge Revaluation is an option. This is a more serious and expensive process where your paper is evaluated by a panel of senior examiners. A portion of the significantly higher fee might be refunded if a substantial change in marks proves a gross error in initial evaluation.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p>It's crucial to remember that VTU enforces strict deadlines for both photocopy and revaluation applications. Students with concerns about their marks are advised to contact their respective college examination cells or the VTU helpdesk promptly.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Stay Updated</h2>
                    <p>The Visvesvaraya Technological University, established in 1998 and headquartered in Belagavi, Karnataka, is recognized by the University Grants Commission as a statutory state university. Students are always advised to regularly check the official VTU website, vtu.ac.in, and the results portal, results.vtu.ac.in, for the latest announcements, revaluation dates, and other important notifications.</p>
                </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
            
